// Fixture: delete_descendant_incomplete_error
// Rule under test: GDDL Spec v4 §6.6 / §12 phase 8 -- "any non-`delete` instance copying
// from one must still fully resolve by export time." Negative-path companion to
// delete_descendant_completes_and_resolves.gddl: here the gap is never closed.
//
// StatsTemplate leaves `mp` uninitialized (permitted). StatsIncomplete copies
// StatsTemplate, touches `hp` only, and never sets `mp` anywhere in its own body either.
// StatsIncomplete is NOT `delete`, so by export time it must be fully resolved -- it
// isn't, so this must be a compile error, caught at final validation (§12 phase 8),
// not earlier (StatsTemplate itself compiles fine at phases 5-7, same as in the
// incomplete-ok fixture -- the fault only exists on StatsIncomplete's side).

define Stats
	hp = u32
	mp = u32

Stats StatsTemplate delete
	hp = 100
	// mp intentionally left uninitialized -- permitted for a delete template

Stats StatsIncomplete = StatsTemplate
	hp = 200
	// mp is still never set anywhere in this chain. StatsIncomplete is not `delete`,
	// so this must fail -- but only at phase 8 (final export validation), not at
	// phases 5-7, since nothing before export attempts to read mp's value.

// Expected (prediction, pending golden output from Compiler Core reference run):
//   Compile error against StatsIncomplete, reported at phase 8 (final validation):
//   field `mp` required for export but never initialized.
//   StatsTemplate itself must NOT be reported as an error source -- the fault is
//   StatsIncomplete's, per the collect-and-report policy (§12 phase 6): a direct
//   failure is recorded once, against the instance where it actually occurs.
